{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human","id":584424,"title":"Changelings becoming human?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T02:43:47-07:00","id":584424,"title":"Changelings becoming human?","content":"<i>Equinox Road</i> describes how a Changeling can reach Wyrd 10 and then transform into one of the Gentry. Would it be possible for a changeling to reduce her Wyrd to zero and become human again? Will either of these be possible in 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:37:27-07:00","id":584772,"title":"","content":"I can't speak to whether these possibilities will be discussed in the 2nd edition book, but stuff like this is generally beyond the scope of the normal rules anyway. If it's possible for a Changeling to become fully human once more, it would presumably require the kind of legendary feat that a whole chronicle could be built around. There <i>has</i> been some discussion of &quot;Icons&quot; in second edition, which seem to be things that a Changeling left behind in Arcadia when they escaped, and I imagine that regaining one's humanity would involve recovering those.<br /> <br /> In first edition, <i>Autumn Nightmares </i>presented the possibility of a Changeling merging with their Fetch, and thereby reclaiming the piece of their soul that their Keeper used in creating the Fetch. That seems like another reasonable prerequisite to reclaiming one's humanity. The Changeling would probably need to undergo some kind of quest in the Hedge as well, since the thorns themselves may have town away portions of their soul as they were carried off to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-09-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:34:09-07:00","id":584865,"title":"","content":"If such a thing were possible, you would probably need a Clarity rating of 10 in order to completely suppress your memories of Arcadia. Similar principle to Golconda, in which you utterly deny your Beast.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd isn't just having access to magical abilities, it is the essence of Arcadia itself. It has bonded with you, filling in the gaps of your soul that were torn away when you were captured. That means in order to remove it, you're going to have be torn apart <i>again</i> so that your human soul can be patched back together. Becoming human should neither be easy nor pleasant, kind of like somebody going through rehabilitation after experiencing a traumatic event.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-09-2015, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:37:15-07:00","id":584868,"title":"","content":"It would be out of theme for changelings to become human again. There's a reality to not being able to go back, only being able to go forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:30:13-07:00","id":585201,"title":"","content":"Regaining humanity doesn't <i>need</i> to mean that they forget Arcadia or their travails in the past. In fact, for the most part, in 2e, given the tight correlation twixt Integrity and Clarity, most of the change would be returning to a human <i>body</i>. (i.e. losing Seeming or whatever it's called)<br /> <br /> Seems reasonable that they'd retain any Contracts not specifically granted to Changelings or Fae, but probably lose the tie to the Wyrd. It would certainly need to be different. Is there some form of enchanted humanity in one of the books that would be a good model to start with? I could see them losing the ability to swear oaths or not, either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:47:23-07:00","id":585239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=585201#post585201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regaining humanity doesn't <i>need</i> to mean that they forget Arcadia or their travails in the past. In fact, for the most part, in 2e, given the tight correlation twixt Integrity and Clarity, most of the change would be returning to a human <i>body</i>. (i.e. losing Seeming or whatever it's called)<br /> <br /> Seems reasonable that they'd retain any Contracts not specifically granted to Changelings or Fae, but probably lose the tie to the Wyrd. It would certainly need to be different. Is there some form of enchanted humanity in one of the books that would be a good model to start with? I could see them losing the ability to swear oaths or not, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fae-Touched spring to mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:56:11-07:00","id":585249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=585239#post585239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fae-Touched spring to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Figured there had to be something. Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:01:33-07:00","id":585265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=585201#post585201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regaining humanity doesn't <i>need</i> to mean that they forget Arcadia or their travails in the past. In fact, for the most part, in 2e, given the tight correlation twixt Integrity and Clarity, most of the change would be returning to a human <i>body</i>. (i.e. losing Seeming or whatever it's called)<br /> <br /> Seems reasonable that they'd retain any Contracts not specifically granted to Changelings or Fae, but probably lose the tie to the Wyrd. It would certainly need to be different. Is there some form of enchanted humanity in one of the books that would be a good model to start with? I could see them losing the ability to swear oaths or not, either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha. No.<br /> <br /> In Universe, the Contracts <i>are</i> the Wyrd. They are done by those powers.<br /> <br /> Out of universe, You will always be marked by your trauma. You don't just get over it. You deal with it for the rest of your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:21:09-07:00","id":585278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=585249#post585249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Figured there had to be something. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> In 2nd E, the Fae Touched are humans that made a significant promise to somebody who became a Changeling and maintained that promise even after they were taken. They are mystically drawn to seek out the Changeling to whom they are bonded, causing them to wander their way through the Hedge and into Arcadia. Somehow they manage to escape without becoming Changelings, but they still have some level of connection to the Wyrd, being allowed to access Contracts and see the true forms of the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:06:02-07:00","id":586273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=585265#post585265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha. No.<br /> <br /> In Universe, the Contracts <i>are</i> the Wyrd. They are done by those powers.<br /> <br /> Out of universe, You will always be marked by your trauma. You don't just get over it. You deal with it for the rest of your life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd be really uncomfortable with the idea of a Changeling becoming human again because of the implications that has when taken in the context of the trauma metaphor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T12:39:47-07:00","id":586357,"title":"","content":"Proud of all your scars. All I have to say on the matter.<br /> <br /> .....<br /> <br /> Okay, not all. In a real way, there's kind of a &quot;end game&quot; in similar vein. The Lost are called that because they feel that they can never quite go home, that things are never the same. I have nothing against running a story where they merge with their fetch, and then happily settle back into human life, get a Happily Ever After where the Gentry don't bother them any more. <br /> <br /> Its not -quite- the same as becoming human, more like the equivalent of achieving Apothesis in Mummy, but it is close enough that I think its an appropriate enough Golconda-esk story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:00:31-07:00","id":589033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=584772#post584772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak to whether these possibilities will be discussed in the 2nd edition book, but stuff like this is generally beyond the scope of the normal rules anyway. If it's possible for a Changeling to become fully human once more, it would presumably require the kind of legendary feat that a whole chronicle could be built around. There <i>has</i> been some discussion of &quot;Icons&quot; in second edition, which seem to be things that a Changeling left behind in Arcadia when they escaped, and I imagine that regaining one's humanity would involve recovering those.<br /> <br /> In first edition, <i>Autumn Nightmares </i>presented the possibility of a Changeling merging with their Fetch, and thereby reclaiming the piece of their soul that their Keeper used in creating the Fetch. That seems like another reasonable prerequisite to reclaiming one's humanity. The Changeling would probably need to undergo some kind of quest in the Hedge as well, since the thorns themselves may have town away portions of their soul as they were carried off to Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would eliminate Changelings without an extant Fetch. Becoming a True Fae doesn't require a legendary feat, just achieving Wyrd 10 and waiting for your Clarity to drop to zero. I was thinking of something symmetric with that since both would be end games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=584865#post584865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If such a thing were possible, you would probably need a Clarity rating of 10 in order to completely suppress your memories of Arcadia. Similar principle to Golconda, in which you utterly deny your Beast.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd isn't just having access to magical abilities, it is the essence of Arcadia itself. It has bonded with you, filling in the gaps of your soul that were torn away when you were captured. That means in order to remove it, you're going to have be torn apart <i>again</i> so that your human soul can be patched back together. Becoming human should neither be easy nor pleasant, kind of like somebody going through rehabilitation after experiencing a traumatic event.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way to reduce Wyrd is given in the core rules on pp. 87-88, requiring going cold turkey from Glamour except the minimum to avoid deprivation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=584868#post584868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be out of theme for changelings to become human again. There's a reality to not being able to go back, only being able to go forward.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=586273#post586273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd be really uncomfortable with the idea of a Changeling becoming human again because of the implications that has when taken in the context of the trauma metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's beginning to sound like an ideology, not a game. Going back from Wyrd 10 is necessary if you want to retain your character. Can't trauma be overcome, esp. in an endgame scenario? One of the biggest criticisms of Lost people have is that they don't want to play a victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:24:38-07:00","id":589044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=589033#post589033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Becoming a True Fae doesn't require a legendary feat</div> </div> </div> </div>Well <i>of course</i> it doesn't. If it did then it would almost never happen. Becoming Nightmare is changeling's Bad End. It's not something most of them would actively strive for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:25:29-07:00","id":589045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=589033#post589033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's beginning to sound like an ideology, not a game. Going back from Wyrd 10 is necessary if you want to retain your character. Can't trauma be overcome, esp. in an endgame scenario? One of the biggest criticisms of Lost people have is that they don't want to play a victim.</div> </div> </div> </div> Trauma can be overcome. But overcoming trauma doesn't get rid of your scars. You are still irrevocably <i>changed</i> by the experience. Going backwards is denial, not overcoming your problems.<br /> <br /> In a real way, Lost is a game about overcoming that trauma and finding your way home. But things will never be the same again. Life moves on, it doesn't pause and wait for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:24:36-07:00","id":589166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=586273#post586273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd be really uncomfortable with the idea of a Changeling becoming human again because of the implications that has when taken in the context of the trauma metaphor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realistically this would be the case. You can forgive and overcome but not really forget or turn back into what you were before. On the other hand this is a storytelling game so a better question to ask is not how it can be accommodated using the system but rather, if that's the kind of story a troupe wants to tell, what's the best way to go about it?<br /> <br /> Note that I agree that it isn't something that should be possible, as MCN notes further below (or above this particular post) you can overcome trauma but you still bear the scars. Nevertheless, a lot of stories gloss over this (just look at the recovery / &quot;return to normalcy&quot; that Fitz went through during the course of AoS season 2 -- people with brain injuries (or a lot of other kinds of injuries) don't return to &quot;normal&quot;). Even if it's against the preferences of some of us, I don't see a problem with speculating as to how the game can be used to accommodate such a story. As has been pointed out, it'd probably look like Vampire's Golconda. IIRC, oWoD Changeling actually had a bunch of rules and text devoted to answering this question. You (the original poster) might want to have a look-see at that material for ideas how it might be adapted to the Lost. Most likely it'll be combination of factors (recovering bits of soul from the Hedge, reducing Wyrd to 1, and increasing Clarity to 8+).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:01:29-07:00","id":589206,"title":"","content":"I guess that if the creators of Changeling ever had to weigh in on the issue in an actual book, what we would probably get is a side bar or something similar that makes it clear this is a game about Loss. It's right there in the name. It's not a Loss if it doesn't change something about you. Representing the changeling condition/viewpoint as something that can be 100% fixed could be misconstrued as being insensitive toward real life trauma. On the other end, implying or even saying that you are Forever Lost is a foolish move as well, because it can make real people who are trying to deal with their traumas think it's pointless, even if this thought is relatively brief. That can be a very dangerous perspective for someone who is already very hurt, no matter how brief. They'd compromise and suggest something along the lines of what MCN said. &quot;Earn Your Happy Ending&quot;, as TV Tropes would put it. The key word here is &quot;suggest&quot;, as is normal for the NWOD.<br /> <br /> Some people like to play the role of the one who tries to deal with tragedy.<br /> <br /> Others like to play the role of the one who gives the middle finger to the Gentry, proceeding to kick ass on the way to building their own Hedge Domain or something similarly defiant.<br /> <br /> Both can be cathartic and reinvigorating in their own ways. Neither are necessarily and inherently wrong.<br /> <br /> So, being game developers, they need to make their games as fun as possible for many people. That requires them to admit the validity of multiple gaming styles. It's the sensible approach to their business. Nobody ever seriously claimed that you can't have a Rogue Trader-like game where you play as a motley of Loyalists with claws and tendrils on lots of shadier-than-average Goblin Markets. You would be playing a role that is abhorrent in the eyes of the standard protagonists, which some would call &quot;missing the point of the game&quot;. But the OPTION to do that should be in there. More stuff to do is very unlikely to be received with nothing but boos and ah-hell-naws.<br /> <br /> Just my two cents. Correct me if you wish to, I'm all ears. Have at thee! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:07:36-07:00","id":589220,"title":"","content":"You know who might actually be able to make a changeling completely human?<br /> <br /> One of the Gentry. <br /> <br /> Loyalist backstory, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:21:33-07:00","id":589230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=589220#post589220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know who might actually be able to make a changeling completely human?<br /> <br /> One of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> Loyalist backstory, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It can be more horrifying than that.<br /> <br /> Said Loyalist might not even be planning on using this one dose cure on himself, but his significant other who is also a changeling who can't maintain a grip on Clarity and rebuild life no matter how hard they try. Desperation is the best leverage in a Pledge, as far as the Gentry are concerned. It makes the fire consuming the circus later on all the prettier.<br /> <br /> And if the Loyalist is not<i> supremely </i>cunning, his loved one might go from changeling to something that is technically human from that Gentry's warped perspective, but most certainly not from the perspective of the Loyalist.<br /> <br /> And then the Gentry politely tells the Loyalist to read the fine print more closely next time, not even bothering to cackle evilly as it returns to the Hedge. Nothing it can do right now will increase the half-breed's exquisite suffering.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T01:31:50-07:00","id":590022,"title":"","content":"I don't know how it would work in 2ed, but in 1ed there was something similar-Winter Masques, I think. Changeling could go to Hedge, and strip parts of their Mien. They could never become human, however they could lessen changes-example, changeling that was turned in humanoid goat could gain feet and lose horns. Downside was that your Wyrd dropped, and you activated Contracts harder.<br /> But getting rid of Wyrd would be hard. It is presented as essence of everything, force that binds nature and ideas together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T04:13:11-07:00","id":592498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=589166#post589166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Realistically this would be the case. You can forgive and overcome but not really forget or turn back into what you were before. On the other hand this is a storytelling game so a better question to ask is not how it can be accommodated using the system but rather, if that's the kind of story a troupe wants to tell, what's the best way to go about it?<br /> <br /> Note that I agree that it isn't something that should be possible, as MCN notes further below (or above this particular post) you can overcome trauma but you still bear the scars. Nevertheless, a lot of stories gloss over this (just look at the recovery / &quot;return to normalcy&quot; that Fitz went through during the course of AoS season 2 -- people with brain injuries (or a lot of other kinds of injuries) don't return to &quot;normal&quot;). Even if it's against the preferences of some of us, I don't see a problem with speculating as to how the game can be used to accommodate such a story. As has been pointed out, it'd probably look like Vampire's Golconda. IIRC, oWoD Changeling actually had a bunch of rules and text devoted to answering this question. You (the original poster) might want to have a look-see at that material for ideas how it might be adapted to the Lost. Most likely it'll be combination of factors (recovering bits of soul from the Hedge, reducing Wyrd to 1, and increasing Clarity to 8+).</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling: the Dreaming changelings were never pure human, but hybrids and body-swappers. There was a state similar to Golconda called Siochain(sp) where a Changeling could balance his fae and human sides, and escape Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T05:13:41-07:00","id":592536,"title":"","content":"There are a couple of ways for a changeling to become a human in the world of darkness that I can think of offhand.<br /> <br /> 1) Go to the underworld, dive into the ocean of fragments until you lose your identity as a changeling. Of course one risks coming out a human of a different age, gender, political idealogy, handedness, ethnicity, nationality, sexuality, height, body type, and every other identifier, so one runs the risk of it being a really creative form of suicide.<br /> <br /> 2) Die and be resurrected by a spirit with that resurrection numen, the one that downgrades supernaturals to their minor template form, so the changeling would probably become fae touched.<br /> <br /> 3) Get an archmaster to remove the template, but that would require, thanks to the pax arcana, the permission of a true fae to do so.<br /> <br /> 4) Get the help of some hunters, in hunter curing monsters is something that, with the ST's permission, can work. Magical ritual, science, miracles?<br /> <br /> 5) Use the couch of dream time travel from GMC to prevent oneself from being taken by the Fae in the first place, although that runs the risk of the character fading away from temporal paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T03:25:48-07:00","id":600316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=592536#post592536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a couple of ways for a changeling to become a human in the world of darkness that I can think of offhand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3) Get an archmaster to remove the template, but that would require, thanks to the pax arcana, the permission of a true fae to do so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Pax Arcana applies to archmages, and only to the world at large, not an individual.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T08:26:26-07:00","id":600594,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I dont see the problem.<br /> I think Vampire and Changeling has a certain degree of common ground in this regard, in the sense that both types has had something tangible done to them, that cant easily be reserved however much they might wish it so. I think it'de be interesting to have it as a possibillity. The Gentry took something from you, to make you a Changeling. Take it back!<br /> <br /> In the context of the metaphor or 'message', I think we could all benefit from remembering that a game like this is a merger between what one wishes to say metaphorically and whats interesting to play out, while also keeping in mind several interpritations of those things. Some people might subscribe to the idea that trauma cannot be overcome and put behind oneself in this fashion and other might people might take an opposite view. I think the games possibillity space could include both of those interpritations and the gamestyles that spring from them. Thats how one creates an enjoyable experience centered around a common theme. To allow the game to express all possible interpritations of those themes and not just one particular one, which oneself subscribes to. You should never try to force people to play something, specific. Yes, Changeling is a game about loss and trauma, but loss and trauma means something different to different people.<br /> I dont think we will be hurting anybody by allowing that multiplicity, and if we somehow end up offending some delicate snowflake, then thats no fault of the writers or any of us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T23:38:59-07:00","id":606393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=600316#post600316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Pax Arcana applies to archmages, and only to the world at large, not an individual.</div> </div> </div> </div> The pax arcanum prevents any use of &quot;imperial spells to directly attack the interests of any other beings covered by it.&quot; <br /> <br /> &quot;All supernatural beings with greater templates..have sponsors in the ascension war who actively prevent archmages from meddling with their agents. These entities will sometimes...permit an archmaster to transform a human into one of their charges.&quot;<br /> <br /> So too reiterate, turning a changeling into a human without the permission of a changeling's sponsor, who would undoubtedly be the Gentry, would be a violation of the Pax Arcanum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T02:40:47-07:00","id":606442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=600594#post600594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I dont see the problem.<br /> I think Vampire and Changeling has a certain degree of common ground in this regard, in the sense that both types has had something tangible done to them, that cant easily be reserved however much they might wish it so. I think it'de be interesting to have it as a possibillity. The Gentry took something from you, to make you a Changeling. Take it back!<br /> <br /> In the context of the metaphor or 'message', I think we could all benefit from remembering that a game like this is a merger between what one wishes to say metaphorically and whats interesting to play out, while also keeping in mind several interpritations of those things. Some people might subscribe to the idea that trauma cannot be overcome and put behind oneself in this fashion and other might people might take an opposite view. I think the games possibillity space could include both of those interpritations and the gamestyles that spring from them. Thats how one creates an enjoyable experience centered around a common theme. To allow the game to express all possible interpritations of those themes and not just one particular one, which oneself subscribes to. You should never try to force people to play something, specific. Yes, Changeling is a game about loss and trauma, but loss and trauma means something different to different people.<br /> I dont think we will be hurting anybody by allowing that multiplicity, and if we somehow end up offending some delicate snowflake, then thats no fault of the writers or any of us.</div> </div> </div> </div> I do agree that someone who despairs and does self-destructive things because of something they read in the rule book of an RPG needs to get a grip. However, I think that maybe I wasn't clear enough in my post at the top of the page. Let me illustrate. If I go overboard, please tell me and I'll be more careful.<br /> <br /> Loyalists can be bad, but also unfortunate. Is your reason for showing up at the game table to participate in the creation of a Tragedy? Go ahead, it's not my business to demand you conform to my tastes. Saying that the content of Changeling or another NWOD game triggered you won't rally serious people to your cause. It will rally whiners.<br /> <br /> Loyalists can be bad, but also repentant. Is your reason for showing up at the game table to participate in the creation of a <b><a href=\"http://condor.depaul.edu/dsimpson/tlove/comic-tragic.html\" target=\"_blank\">Comedy</a></b>? <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Go ahead, it's not my business to demand you conform to my tastes. Saying that the content of Changeling or another NWOD game triggered you won't rally serious people to your cause. It will rally assholes.<br /> <br /> See what I mean more clearly now?</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-29-2015, 05:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:55:18-07:00","id":609446,"title":"","content":"May I suggest an alternative to the usual: Genius the Transgression. In the book, one of the devices you can build at Metatpropi 3 can change the shape of living creatures temporarily, but investing a point of Mania into the transformation will make it hold I believe. However, a shape shifted Changeling-turned-human is still a changeling in essence, unfortunately. Genii can cheat reality and do the impossible if only for a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:33:45-07:00","id":609605,"title":"","content":"So it's not really a human, it's a changeling held in the shape of a human. Which they can do with Contracts.<br /> <br /> So it's kind of worthless.<br /> <br /> ....Not the best argument I've seen for Genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:41:46-07:00","id":609609,"title":"","content":"<i>Step right up, Step right up. I got some human beans here! 100% human beans. Wishing to recapture that good old humanity? Just eat these and bam! Hehe, you are what you eat after all. Just a quick snack will set you right.<br /> <br /> notavailableinallareastermsandconditionsapplyassta tedintheundocumentedcontractconsumingbeansdoesnotk eepthegentryoffyourbackyoushouldknowthis.alltrades finalandnofuggingrefunded.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T09:51:14-07:00","id":609618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human#post584424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Equinox Road</i> describes how a Changeling can reach Wyrd 10 and then transform into one of the Gentry. Would it be possible for a changeling to reduce her Wyrd to zero and become human again? Will either of these be possible in 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd say no. What happened to you can't NOT have happened to you (sans time travel). You can take power back and redefine your life afterwards (which is what Seeming and Courts etc all represent now), but it can't not have an impact. You are &quot;changed&quot; - but retain the ability to define the change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:41:53-07:00","id":609791,"title":"","content":"I hope they are addressed with possibility / impossibility being left to the individual troupes and storytellers. Honestly, would it be so bad if it came with the price of &quot;the old you is gone, it had to go so that the new you could be&quot; -- this is essentially how C.S. Friedmans Coldfire Trilogy ends for one of the two protagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 07-31-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:11:05-07:00","id":609816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=609791#post609791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope they are addressed with possibility / impossibility being left to the individual troupes and storytellers. Honestly, would it be so bad if it came with the price of &amp;quot;the old you is gone, it had to go so that the new you could be&amp;quot; -- this is essentially how C.J. Cherryh's Coldfire Trilogy ends for one of the two protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not what I want in a Changeling game. If others want it in their games that's fine. I think &quot;it's up to the troupe/ST&quot; goes without saying, though. I'm more interested in discussing the merits of allowing or not allowing it - just because I don't think it suits the themes of Changeling doesn't mean it's not valuable for me to hear why others do think it fits, and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:13:16-07:00","id":610018,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the problem. IIRC, Changeling magic always has built in prices. What I'm describing above is ...and you became human, but not that character, that character ceased to exist and now you have a new character that is human. All that trauma and all the memories of that trauma -- zapped away. Of course you should have to pay a steep price storywise for that. Think of the story arcs in Full Metal Alchemist. Could be an epic story indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T22:53:55-07:00","id":610434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/584424-changelings-becoming-human?p=610018#post610018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see the problem. IIRC, Changeling magic always has built in prices. What I'm describing above is ...and you became human, but not that character, that character ceased to exist and now you have a new character that is human. All that trauma and all the memories of that trauma -- zapped away. Of course you should have to pay a steep price storywise for that. Think of the story arcs in Full Metal Alchemist. Could be an epic story indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't like what that says about dealing with trauma. Just become someone else and everything that happened to you gets erased along with your old self? No, I don't think that's healthy, and I don't think it's what Changeling is about. The way I see it, Changeling is about learning to live <i>with</i> what happened, not escape it. Wanting to just erase your old life and start over as a whole new person is a great place for a character's motivation to start from, but that should only be the first step in their character development arc - a desire they have to overcome before they can learn to accept themselves as they are, not something to be achieved. FMA spoilers ahead.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Remember, Ed was only able to get Al's soul back by sacrificing his own ability to do alchemy, and along with it, any chance he may have had at repairing his own body. He had to make the choice to accept himself as he was, including his responsibility for what happened to them both, in order to make amends to Al. I don't think that would have been anywhere near as powerful if they had just found some way to use alchemy to undo their past.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-01-2015, 02:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}